    {
      "name": "4. OAuth Integration",
      "disabled": true,
      "description": "Smoke tests for OAuth 2.0 provider initiation endpoints (Google and LinkedIn).\n\n### Why Only Initiation Endpoints?\nOAuth callback endpoints (`/auth/:provider/callback`) require a real one-time authorization `code` issued by the provider after the user completes the browser consent flow. This code:\n- Cannot be generated or predicted programmatically\n- Expires within seconds and can only be used once\n- Requires an active browser session with the OAuth provider\n\nTherefore, callback testing is excluded from this smoke suite. Complete OAuth callback testing is covered in `test/oauth.e2e-spec.ts` using mocked guards and a real database.\n\n### Newman Cookie Isolation\nAll OAuth initiation tests clear the cookie jar before execution to prevent any auth cookies from a previous login step from leaking into these requests.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/unsupported-provider - Unsupported OAuth Provider (400 Bad Request)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Clear cookies from the cookie jar before this unauthenticated request.",
                  "// Newman's cookie jar persists cookies across requests by default, which can cause false positives.",
                  "pm.cookies.clear();",
                  "pm.request.headers.remove('Cookie');"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 400 Bad Request for unsupported provider', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Response contains unsupported provider message', function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.message).to.include('is not supported');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/unsupported-provider",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "unsupported-provider"]
            }
          }
        },
